{"entity": "Firmware Update", "type": "method", "description": "Firmware update is a post-installation process recommended after OS installation to ensure optimal performance.<SEP>Firmware update refers to the process of applying updated firmware files to support GPU hardware functionality.<SEP>Firmware update involves refreshing kernel modules and device tree blobs to fix system issues on VisionFive.<SEP>Firmware Update is a process triggered to apply a new firmware version to the BMC, typically initiated through one of several supported methods.<SEP>Firmware Update is the process of upgrading the low-level software embedded in hardware components such as BMC or BIOS.<SEP>Firmware Update is a procedure for upgrading the BMC firmware using a USB storage device."}
