{"entity": "openEuler 24.03 LTS SP1", "type": "version", "description": "openEuler 24.03 LTS SP1 is a specific long-term support (LTS) release version of the openEuler operating system, based on the Linux kernel 6.6, designed for extended maintenance and stability across diverse deployment scenarios. This release supports multiple architectures and is intended for use in server, cloud, edge computing, and embedded environments. As an enhanced version of the 24.03 LTS release, it incorporates improvements in system reliability, security, and performance, making it suitable as a foundational platform for software installation, development, and production workloads. It has been successfully updated and released, undergoing documentation center restructuring to improve accessibility and usability. Users leverage openEuler 24.03 LTS SP1 for various purposes, including the installation of applications such as MongoDB via Docker, system configuration, and software development. While it is primarily used for stable, long-term operations, some users have reported encountering issues during Xfce desktop installation and problems with Chinese character display in the shell environment. Additionally, this release is used in testing scenarios to avoid out-of-memory (OOM) issues, indicating its utility in controlled and resource-sensitive contexts. Overall, openEuler 24.03 LTS SP1 represents a mature, well-supported distribution tailored for enterprise-grade and large-scale deployments.<SEP>openEuler 24.03 LTS SP1 is the operating system version where the issue with missing commands in libguestfs was observed."}
