{"entity": "openEuler Community", "type": "organization", "description": "The openEuler Community is a global, collaborative open-source initiative dedicated to the development, maintenance, and distribution of the openEuler operating system. It functions as the official community responsible for creating, supporting, and releasing openEuler versions, including SP2 and other major releases. The community operates under the Open Atoms Open Source Foundation and serves as a collective platform for developers, users, contributors, and partners from diverse organizations and regions. It emphasizes collaboration, innovation, and cross-architecture support, with growing interest in the RISC-V ecosystem. The openEuler Community develops and maintains a stable, secure, and high-performance Linux distribution tailored for enterprise servers and diverse computing scenarios. It hosts thousands of software repositories and provides a fully integrated ecosystem, including tools like DevKit, QEMU virtual machine images in qcow2 format, and Distroless container images. The community manages critical infrastructure components such as the metalink service and the artlfs service for large file storage. Special Interest Groups (SIGs) play a central role in organizing technical work, with active participation in areas including security, documentation, system compatibility, and release validation. The community supports software development through structured governance, code collaboration via pull requests, and a robust issue-tracking system. It maintains extensive documentation and resources, including the openEuler documentation map, migration guides, deployment guides, and compatibility documentation. The openEuler Community also publishes an annual report and engages with contributors through events like the FOSSASIA Summit 2023. It manages security information, including the CVE list, and provides expert support for system integration and application development. The project is hosted on Gitee, with rigorous contribution practices such as license agreement compliance. The openEuler Community fosters user exchange, builds regional user groups, collects industry application cases, and promotes the adoption of openEuler through open forums and communication channels. As a grassroots, globally distributed initiative, it continues to advance foundational software and drive innovation in open-source operating systems.<SEP>The openEuler Community is a collaborative forum for developers and users of the openEuler Linux distribution.<SEP>The openEuler Community is an open-source initiative managing the openEuler operating system and its ecosystem."}
