{"entity": "OpenEuler Community", "type": "organization", "description": "OpenEuler Community is a global collaborative open-source organization dedicated to the development, governance, maintenance, and promotion of the openEuler operating system. As the central hub of the openEuler ecosystem, the community functions as a collective network of developers, contributors, and organizations from around the world who work together to advance the open-source operating system. It oversees the entire lifecycle of the project, including technical design, version maintenance, security updates, and release coordination. The community is responsible for establishing and enforcing contribution workflows, governance models, and community rules to ensure sustainable and transparent development. It supports the openEuler operating system through the provision of official ISO images, comprehensive documentation, security announcements, and developer resources. The OpenEuler Community also fosters innovation through specialized working groups known as Special Interest Groups (SIGs), which focus on particular aspects of the operating system. Hosting forums and collaborative spaces—such as the official site www.openeuler.openatom.cn—the community enables discussion, coordination, and knowledge sharing among its members. Whether through direct code contributions, testing, or advocacy, the OpenEuler Community plays a central role in sustaining and evolving the openEuler project as a robust, secure, and enterprise-ready open-source platform."}
