{"entity": "OpenUBMC", "type": "organization", "description": "OpenUBMC is an open-source community project and organization dedicated to the development and deployment of Baseboard Management Controller (BMC) software, serving as a foundational platform for hardware and storage system management. It functions as a comprehensive software framework that enables white-label customization and provides a unified interface for managing diverse hardware components, particularly within data center and enterprise environments. Central to its architecture is a modular BMC firmware implementation that supports device discovery via SSDP (Simple Service Discovery Protocol), facilitating seamless network integration and remote access. The platform includes advanced capabilities such as SFF VPD (Smart Fan and Drive Parameter) integration, allowing it to read SSD base information directly from hardware and map it into a hierarchical resource tree for enhanced system visibility.\n\nOpenUBMC supports standardized system telemetry and diagnostics through a Configuration Service Request (CSR) mechanism, enabling consistent monitoring and configuration across managed devices. It also incorporates a structured logging system that records detailed operational data, critical for troubleshooting, auditing, and system maintenance. The platform includes a RAID southbound component driver, contributing to the standardization of storage management within BMC-enabled systems. Additionally, OpenUBMC offers observability solutions enhanced by integrated visualization backends, supporting real-time monitoring and performance analysis.\n\nSecurity is a core priority, with the platform supporting dual signing algorithms — RSA and SM2 — ensuring robust authentication and integrity verification for firmware updates and system operations. It also features DDNS (Dynamic DNS) functionality, improving remote accessibility and manageability of systems across distributed networks. The project is actively maintained through an open-source model, with an official website at https://www.openubmc.cn/ serving as a central hub for documentation, source code access, and community collaboration. While OpenUBMC is primarily recognized for its BMC management tools, firmware, and system integration features, it also provides comprehensive documentation on product development and multi-level customization, supporting both enterprise and developer use cases.<SEP>OpenUBMC is the open-source organization hosting the hardware-sig repositories."}
