ure, including compatibility, dependency resolution, and configuration integrity. The term 'Upgrade' thus denotes a multifaceted, system-critical operation central to modern system maintenance, currently in a pending or partially completed state across several instances.<SEP>The upgrade process involves updating system software or firmware, including rebuilding boot components.<SEP>Upgrade refers to the process of updating firmware, requiring adequate space on the Flash Chip."}
