{"entity": "OpenEuler 22.03", "type": "version", "description": "OpenEuler 22.03 is a specific release version of the OpenEuler operating system, designated as LTS-SP1, and serves as a long-term support release intended for enterprise environments. It is a Linux-based distribution that supports both x86_64 and aarch64 architectures, with kernel version 5.10.0-60.18.0.50.oe2203.aarch64 specifically noted in some deployments. Used as a foundation for EulerOS 2.12, it is targeted for system installation, deployment, and software package management, including compiling and installing OpenSSH 9.8p1, as well as supporting the Wlnmp source and running KVM virtualization. It has been deployed on cloud servers, valued for its stability and community-driven development, and is used in contexts involving PostgreSQL and PostGIS setups, dual-boot systems with LVM, and network configuration testing.\n\nThe release is associated with both successful and problematic behaviors across various use cases. It successfully generated a working OpenSSH 9.8 RPM package and supports Isula-Build execution without failure. However, it has exhibited several issues, including a system startup failure when FIPS mode is enabled, performance degradation in C++ services compared to CentOS 7.6, and low CPU utilization in specific services. Additionally, users have reported that port 8002 cannot be properly closed after process termination, input commands are not displayed after typing, and certain packages such as `fmt` and `libguestfs-winsupport` are unavailable in official repositories, requiring manual compilation or alternative methods.\n\nOther reported challenges include problems with GlusterFS, where hard links cannot be created despite available storage, network interface initialization issues that were later resolved in this version, and difficulties installing Docker due to incompatibility with some CentOS 8.4 packages. The system lacks a default Chinese character set, and users have encountered unusual journal logging behavior during kernel crash troubleshooting. It was also used as a source system for upgrades and as the target OS after migrating from CentOS 7.6/7.9, though it was noted that Wi-Fi configuration worked correctly in this version. OpenEuler 22.03 is also used in contexts involving MLNX_OFED_LINUX support and driver version reporting during system testing.<SEP>OpenEuler 22.03 is a version of the OpenEuler operating system where xrdp functions normally without black screen issues."}
